[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Authored full unit test suite for semver_solver_impl: VersionEngine parse_version/compare_precedence/parse_range/satisfies happy paths and every contracted error branch (InvalidVersionError, InvalidRangeError), PackageRepository registration/descending ordering/missing-package/copy semantics, and DependencySolver highest-precedence resolution plus root, transitive, and missing-package ResolutionConflictError branches; all tests run in an active system lifecycle phase scope.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver.py: Implement interface module: exceptions as mutable dataclasses with message rendering, frozen data types with concrete Version.format/is_prerelease/__str__ and VersionRange.__str__, and abstract VersionEngine/PackageRepository/DependencySolver protocols with stub operations.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Implement SemVer 2.0.0 engine (regex version parsing with leading-zero rejection, precedence comparison, range compilation to DNF comparators with comparators/caret/tilde/wildcard/hyphen/union support and prerelease filtering), descending-sorted package repository, and MRV backtracking dependency solver raising ResolutionConflictError without leaking PackageNotFoundError.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: [slug:semver.repo.register_release] [viol:test.lifecycle_registration_omitted] Facet: inactive phase scope in test setup Witness: phase=system, obs=LifecycleResolutionError('No singleton registered for VersionEngine'). SemverLifecycleTestCase.setUp (lines 30-36) constructs the system phase scope with enter_phase(system, registry=self.registry) but never enters or activates it, so operations that resolve collaborators through the ambient singleton context in PackageRepositoryTest and DependencySolverTest fall back to the empty global registry and fail with LifecycleResolutionError before any contracted behavior runs. The required pattern in support/lib/lifecycle.pyi is that unit tests initialize the target module and resolve singletons within an active lifecycle phase scope entered via 'with enter_phase(...) as scope'; the scope must be active for the whole test so the semver.repo.register_release, semver.repo.descending_releases, semver.solver.compatible_assignment, semver.solver.highest_precedence, and semver.solver.unsatisfiable_conflict postconditions are actually exercised.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Fixed lifecycle registration feedback: every test method now enters an active phase scope via 'with enter_phase(system, registry=self.registry) as scope' and resolves VersionEngine, PackageRepository, and DependencySolver from that active scope, so PackageRepository/DependencySolver ambient get_singleton collaborator resolution targets the test registry instead of the empty global registry and no longer raises LifecycleResolutionError before contracted behavior runs.
